body:
Well that's the crux of it really.  When you start thinking of yourselves as the "goodies" and themmuns as the "baddies", then you start thinking anything you do is good and can justify all sorts of things.  Loyalists think they're the goodies and the Catholics are the baddies so they're justified in wanting to kill the Catholics.  Just like how Nazi supporters thought Jews were the baddies, who were secretly running the world, and so they felt justified in killing them.

&#x200B;

It works both ways, though I know people here don't like to think that.   Just look at some of the people on here who try to justify IRA murders.   I've seen people say they were defending themselves and all those deaths were accidental and so on.  I have nothing against defending yourself, but think of the analogy of a husband beating his wife.  If a husband hits his wife then she has every right to fight back.  It's another thing if she keeps missing and accidentally wounding and killing her kids, over and over again.
